# CHAROS changelog

## Unreleased

- Prepare TC-Nest for NixOS 26.05 by replacing removed `neofetch` with the
  maintained `fastfetch` system-information tool.
- Begin the required durable build and change records for future maintenance.
- Move Node.js from 22 to 24 and remove system-wide heavyweight ML libraries;
  keep lightweight audio and web-service Python dependencies in the base OS.
- Keep project code and history while moving heavyweight model dependencies
  out of the host system closure and into isolated, lesson-specific runtimes.
- Reframe TC-Nest documentation around its September 2026 learning-machine
  role and label former resident accounts as migration history to preserve.
- Add a dated storage inventory separating identity, dirty work, and live
  service state from roughly 12 GiB of conservative cleanup candidates.
- Document the official standalone Codex CLI as Nathan's current user-level
  installation while retaining the NixOS package as a declarative fallback.
- Add `cryptsetup` and specify a 128 GiB LUKS2/ext4 preservation container that
  leaves the Portable SSD's existing exFAT data intact.
- Create and recovery-test that encrypted preservation vault; copy the selected
  filesystem state, export live service data consistently, preserve the stopped
  Wolfden container layer, and record checksums plus reconstruction metadata.
- Remove the verified rebuildable cleanup set and retire the legacy Scout
  pipeline services and timers from the active TC-Nest system role.
- Activate NixOS 26.05 as generation 63 through a normal kernel boot, retaining
  generation 62 as the immediate 25.11 rollback and verifying the graphical,
  network, synchronization, container, and learning-toolchain layers.
- Remove NixOS generations 1 through 61 and garbage-collect their unreachable
  store paths, reducing the boot menu to the current and immediate rollback
  generations.
